# Initial Setup's Parachute page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigHWParachute.cs
# (PLAN.md §13.6 row 70).
#
# The claim: Activate shows the output already on function 27 in "Servo Num", sets up "Enable
# (AC3.3+)" on CHUTE_ENABLED, the release type on CHUTE_TYPE from the page's own list of four
# relays and a servo, and the resting, deploy and minimum-altitude numbers on CHUTE_SERVO_OFF,
# CHUTE_SERVO_ON and CHUTE_ALT_MIN (ConfigHWParachute.cs:17-45); each Mavlink* control writes its
# parameter when changed, a number 300 ms after; "Servo Num" runs ensureDisabled and sets the
# chosen output's _FUNCTION to 27 (:47-74). Each write is proved by the vehicle's echo, and put
# back.
#
# SITL's copter, with the parachute off, lists CHUTE_ENABLED alone: the type combo and the three
# numbers are disabled, as a Mavlink* control without its parameter is, and "Servo Num" lists RC9
# to RC14 - names a SERVOn firmware has not got, so it selects nothing. Enable writes 1 and, the
# table not refreshed, the other controls stay as they were; a second click writes 0.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-parachute.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave CHUTE_ENABLED at 1; the first expectation on it then fails
# until a fresh SITL.

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.CHUTE_ENABLED 0

click tab-setup
expect config.parachute.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigHWParachute
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigHWParachute
expect config.parachute.active true
expect config.parachute.heading Parachute

# What Activate made of SITL's parameters.
expect config.parachute.enable unchecked
expect config.parachute.enable.enabled true
expect config.parachute.type.enabled false
expect config.parachute.type.options 5
expect config.parachute.servo none
expect config.parachute.servo.options 6
expect config.parachute.chute_servo_off.enabled false
expect config.parachute.chute_servo_on.enabled false
expect config.parachute.chute_alt_min.enabled false
expect config.parachute.write none

# Enable: the control's write, echoed.
click parachute-CHUTE_ENABLED
settle 3
expect config.parachute.enable checked
expect params.value.CHUTE_ENABLED 1
expect config.parachute.write ~ CHUTE_ENABLED 1
expect config.parachute.writes.pending 0
expect config.parachute.message none

# And back.
click parachute-CHUTE_ENABLED
settle 3
expect config.parachute.enable unchecked
expect params.value.CHUTE_ENABLED 0
expect config.parachute.message none

# Choosing another page hides this one; it is IActivate only.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect config.parachute.active false
